# omk.conf - where this repo's inputs live on THIS machine.
#
# Copy to `omk.conf` (which is gitignored) and edit. Every line is optional;
# anything you leave out falls back to the in-tree default shown beside it.
#
#   key = value      # `#` starts a comment, blank lines are ignored
#
# A relative path is taken relative to the repository root, not to wherever
# you happen to run a tool from, so one config file means the same thing
# everywhere. `~` is expanded.
#
# Precedence, first hit wins:
#     a flag (--data/--asm/--decomp/--clean)  >  the environment  >  this file
#     >  the in-tree default
#
# `python3 tools/omkpaths.py` prints what each one resolved to and why.


# --- the game data --------------------------------------------------------
# Your own copy of Omikron: The Nomad Soul - the directory holding IAM/,
# MESHES/, SCPTDATA/, MORPH/ and `Runtime 2.exe`. Nothing here ships it, and
# most tools need it. Environment: OMK_DATA
#
# data = gamedata
# data = ~/games/omikron/data
# data = /Volumes/OMIKRON1


# --- the disassembly ------------------------------------------------------
# An IDA listing of `Runtime 2.exe`, and the Hex-Rays decompilation beside it.
# A disassembly is a derivative work of the binary, so this repository does
# not distribute one; point at your own if you have produced it.
#
# Without these, 13 of the suite's checks report `skipped` and everything else
# runs normally - `tools/dialog_disasm.py` falls back to the committed
# `tables/vm_opcodes.json`, which carries the same VM table.
#
# Environment: OMK_ASM, OMK_DECOMP, OMK_DECOMP_H
#
# asm    = Runtime.exe.asm
# decomp = Runtime.exe.c
# header = Runtime.exe.h


# --- clean/ ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The mechanical pass `tools/clean.py` makes over the decompilation. Derived
# from it, so it has the same status: not distributed, regenerate it yourself.
# Environment: OMK_CLEAN
#
# clean = clean
